Any V-item failure = STOP. The response then follows
the §3.1 classification: a class A failure (T1–T4
surfaces) proceeds to rollback evaluation under the
§3.2 safety conditions; a class B finding (T5/T6, and
anything causally unresolved) goes to HOLD + preserve
evidence + escalate, with **no rollback inside this
gate**. STOP prevents further operator action
inside the gate; per the standing correction-6
discipline, STOP is never represented as affecting an
alarm chain (none is provoked by C1).

